{"id":"pw2gw","title":"pw2gw.x","program":"pw2gw.x","package":"PWscf","version":"7.5","html":"<section class=\"qe-section qe-sec-intro\" id=\"intro\" data-kind=\"intro\" data-title=\"Introduction\"><h2 class=\"qe-section-title\">Introduction</h2>\n\n<div class=\"qe-indent\"><pre class=\"qe-pre\"><b>Purpose of pw2gw.x:</b>\n   Optical properties in single-particle approach (Fermi Golden Rule).\n   Interface with GW and excitonic codes.</pre>\n<p class=\"qe-flow\">The code computes and writes (\"matrixelements\" file) the optical matrix elemenents in the\ndipole approximation.</p>\n<p class=\"qe-flow\">The code computes the imaginary part of the dielectric tensor xx, yy and zz (\"epsX.dat\", \"epsY.dat\",\n\"epsZ.dat\") and the average (\"epsTOT.dat\")</p>\n<pre class=\"qe-pre\"><b>Structure of the input data:</b>\n============================\n\n<b>&amp;INPUTPP</b>\n  ...\n<b>/</b></pre></div>\n</section>\n   <section class=\"qe-section qe-sec-namelist\" id=\"INPUTPP\" data-kind=\"namelist\" data-title=\"&amp;INPUTPP\" data-name=\"INPUTPP\"><h2 class=\"qe-section-title\"><span class=\"qe-kind\">Namelist</span> <span class=\"qe-nl\">&amp;INPUTPP</span></h2><div class=\"qe-layout\">\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"prefix\" data-var=\"prefix\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#prefix\">prefix</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">STRING</span> <span class=\"qe-status\">MANDATORY</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"prefix\"></span></header><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">the first part of the name of all the file written by the code\nshould be equal to the value given in the main calculations.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"outdir\" data-var=\"outdir\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#outdir\">outdir</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">STRING</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"outdir\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>\"./\"</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">the scratch directory where the massive data-files are written</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"what\" data-var=\"what\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#what\">what</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">STRING</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"what\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>\"gw\"</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">\"gw\" : Calculate dipole optical matrix elements (use for norm-conserving pseudopotentials)\nand imaginary part of the dielectric function.</p>\n<p class=\"qe-flow\">\"gmaps\": write g-maps for each processor in a file \"fort.'100 + processor number'\"</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"qplda\" data-var=\"qplda\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#qplda\">qplda</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">LOGICAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"qplda\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>.FALSE.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">if .TRUE. write the interface file \"QPLDA\" to GW and BSE codes (chisig, dpforexc).</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"vxcdiag\" data-var=\"vxcdiag\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#vxcdiag\">vxcdiag</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">LOGICAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"vxcdiag\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>.FALSE.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">if .TRUE. calculates the expectation value of the exchange and correlation potential\non all the Kohn-Sham states and write it into the \"vxcdiag.dat\" file.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"vkb\" data-var=\"vkb\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#vkb\">vkb</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">LOGICAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"vkb\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>.FALSE.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><pre class=\"qe-pre\">    if .TRUE. use Kleyman-Bylander projectors to write additional informatio into fort.15 file\n(Still in development)</pre></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"Emin\" data-var=\"Emin\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#Emin\">Emin</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"Emin\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>0.0</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Starting photon energy for which the dielectric function is calculated (in eV)</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"Emax\" data-var=\"Emax\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#Emax\">Emax</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"Emax\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>30.0</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Highest photon energy for which the dielectric function is calculated (in eV)</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"DeltaE\" data-var=\"DeltaE\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#DeltaE\">DeltaE</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"DeltaE\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>0.05</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Energy step with which the dielectric function is calculated (in eV)</p></div></article>\n\n   </div></section>","sections":[{"id":"intro","title":"Introduction","kind":"intro","level":0,"varIds":[]},{"id":"INPUTPP","title":"&INPUTPP","kind":"namelist","name":"INPUTPP","level":0,"varIds":["prefix","outdir","what","qplda","vxcdiag","vkb","Emin","Emax","DeltaE"]}],"variables":[{"id":"prefix","names":["prefix"],"display":"prefix","type":"STRING","status":"MANDATORY","sectionId":"INPUTPP","sectionTitle":"&INPUTPP","options":[],"summary":"the first part of the name of all the file written by the code should be equal to the value given in the main calculations."},{"id":"outdir","names":["outdir"],"display":"outdir","type":"STRING","default":"\"./\"","sectionId":"INPUTPP","sectionTitle":"&INPUTPP","options":[],"summary":"the scratch directory where the massive data-files are written"},{"id":"what","names":["what"],"display":"what","type":"STRING","default":"\"gw\"","sectionId":"INPUTPP","sectionTitle":"&INPUTPP","options":[],"summary":"\"gw\" : Calculate dipole optical matrix elements (use for norm-conserving pseudopotentials) and imaginary part of the dielectric function. \"gmaps\": write g-maps for each processor in a file \"fort.'100 + processor number'\""},{"id":"qplda","names":["qplda"],"display":"qplda","type":"LOGICAL","default":".FALSE.","sectionId":"INPUTPP","sectionTitle":"&INPUTPP","options":[],"summary":"if .TRUE. write the interface file \"QPLDA\" to GW and BSE codes (chisig, dpforexc)."},{"id":"vxcdiag","names":["vxcdiag"],"display":"vxcdiag","type":"LOGICAL","default":".FALSE.","sectionId":"INPUTPP","sectionTitle":"&INPUTPP","options":[],"summary":"if .TRUE. calculates the expectation value of the exchange and correlation potential on all the Kohn-Sham states and write it into the \"vxcdiag.dat\" file."},{"id":"vkb","names":["vkb"],"display":"vkb","type":"LOGICAL","default":".FALSE.","sectionId":"INPUTPP","sectionTitle":"&INPUTPP","options":[],"summary":"if .TRUE. use Kleyman-Bylander projectors to write additional informatio into fort.15 file (Still in development)"},{"id":"Emin","names":["Emin"],"display":"Emin","type":"REAL","default":"0.0","sectionId":"INPUTPP","sectionTitle":"&INPUTPP","options":[],"summary":"Starting photon energy for which the dielectric function is calculated (in eV)"},{"id":"Emax","names":["Emax"],"display":"Emax","type":"REAL","default":"30.0","sectionId":"INPUTPP","sectionTitle":"&INPUTPP","options":[],"summary":"Highest photon energy for which the dielectric function is calculated (in eV)"},{"id":"DeltaE","names":["DeltaE"],"display":"DeltaE","type":"REAL","default":"0.05","sectionId":"INPUTPP","sectionTitle":"&INPUTPP","options":[],"summary":"Energy step with which the dielectric function is calculated (in eV)"}],"aliases":{"id3":"prefix","prefix":"prefix","id4":"outdir","outdir":"outdir","id5":"what","what":"what","id6":"qplda","qplda":"qplda","id7":"vxcdiag","vxcdiag":"vxcdiag","id8":"vkb","vkb":"vkb","id9":"Emin","Emin":"Emin","id10":"Emax","Emax":"Emax","id11":"DeltaE","DeltaE":"DeltaE","id2":"INPUTPP","INPUTPP":"INPUTPP","id1":"intro"}}